{
	"_note": "Mio keeps the fish traps and the old ferry on the river south of the village (data/maps/river.json) and lives in her father's driftwood hut on the north bank (data/maps/mio_hut.json). Mornings she works her traps along the shore east of the path (the fishing pose), and at 9:30 on a fine day she takes the old ferry across from her landing and back (a {\"ferry\": 30} step, data/ferry.json; not in winter, when she only looks at it from the shore); lunch at the hut; at 13:00 she takes the lane up through Minamino to sell her catch at the Yorozu Store's front (13:30-14:30); back to mend nets on the gravel by the path until 18:00, at the hut until bed at 21:00. Wet days she mends nets by the stove. On her birthday (spring 12, when the river runs high with snowmelt) no traps and no ferry: she sits on the far east end of the shore 9:00-16:00 watching the far bank. Festivals bring her up to the village for their hours, standing on the south road. Married to the farmer (married_mio, data/marriage.json) she lives at the farmhouse: by the kotatsu in the second room before 6:40 and from 18:00, the river and the store as before in between, and on a wet day she mends nets by the kotatsu. Her heart events: data/events/heart_mio.json (band 3), heart_mio_5.json (band 5), heart_mio_6.json (band 6; after it she can be asked to marry). Gifts: river fish and fish dishes, rice balls and hearty rice; amber from the mine (it washes up in rivers, she says); a moon lantern above all, for night crossings; fancy sweets and matcha are too dainty for her; a plain stone is an insult. A character of our own, one of the four new candidates (docs/DESIGN.md, ความรักและแต่งงาน). Format: README.md, Villagers.",
